\section{The effects table (output, \code{fit$effects})}{

Every fit — either engine, anchored or not — carries a tidy per-drug
effects table with these columns, in this order:
\describe{
\item{\code{drug}}{Character. One row per drug, in network
(alphabetical) order.}
\item{\code{estimate}}{Numeric. The drug's position on the log scale:
relative to \code{reference} for a surface fit, absolute versus
placebo for an anchored fit.}
\item{\code{std_error}}{Numeric. Standard error (netmeta) or posterior
standard deviation (Stan).}
\item{\code{lower}, \code{upper}}{Numeric. 95\% confidence limits (netmeta)
or central 95\% posterior interval (Stan).}
\item{\code{scale}}{Character, always \code{"log"}.}
\item{\code{reference}}{Character. The drug fixed at 0 for a surface
fit; \code{"placebo"} for an anchored fit.}
\item{\code{engine}}{Character, \code{"netmeta"} or \code{"stan"}.}
}
In an unanchored fit the reference drug's row is pinned exactly:
\code{estimate}, \code{std_error}, \code{lower}, and \code{upper} are all 0. Stan fits
append the posterior summary columns \code{median}, \code{mean}, \code{sd}, \code{q025},
\code{q975} and the convergence diagnostics \code{rhat}, \code{ess_bulk},
\code{ess_tail} (\code{NA} on a pinned reference row, which is a constant, not
a sampled quantity).
}

\section{The covariance component (output, \code{fit$covariance})}{

Every fit carries the full covariance matrix of its estimated
effects: one row and column per drug, in the same order as the
effects table, with \code{dimnames} naming the drugs. Both engines supply
the same component in the same shape — the common-effect covariance
of every drug versus the reference (netmeta) or the posterior
covariance of \code{theta} (Stan) — and its diagonal is consistent with
the effects table's \code{std_error} column. In an unanchored fit the
reference drug's row and column are exact zeros (the reference is a
constant); an anchored fit pins no drug, so no row is zero.
Anchoring and the leverage-aware residual standardization consume
this component.
}

\section{The other fit components (output)}{

A \code{directeffect_fit} also carries \code{comparisons} and \code{anchors} (the
input tables, unchanged), \code{heterogeneity} (netmeta: list \code{Q}, \code{df},
\code{p_value}, \code{tau}, \code{I2}; Stan common-effect: list \code{model}, \code{tau}),
\code{diagnostics} (list, reserved), \code{engine}, \code{engine_fit} (the raw
netmeta or stanfit object — the only place engine internals appear),
and \code{network} (the \code{directeffect_network} that was fitted).
}

